    "probe_text": "I now have the full pipeline. Here is every validation and side-effect applied by `POST /api/owners`, in execution order.\n\n## Gate (before the pipeline)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 the whole endpoint requires `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` (`owners.POST.yml` `composition.authorize`). A caller without the role gets `AuthorizationDeniedException` (403).\n\n## Pipeline steps, in order\n\n1. **CheckIdempotencyKey** *(branch)* \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header. If non-blank **and** already recorded in the in-memory `IdempotencyKeyStore`, it branches to **replay**: loads that original owner and responds **200** with it (or **NotFound/404** if it's gone) \u2014 no create happens. Otherwise it proceeds to the create pipeline. *(Side-effect on replay: none; just a read.)*\n\n2. **ValidateRequiredOwnerFields** \u2014 binds the body (no `@Valid`). Normalizes the address (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand abbreviations) via `AddressNormalizer`, choosing structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` if present else the flat `address`. **Validation:** rejects with `MissingRequiredFieldsException` (**400**) if any of *firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone* is missing/blank **after** normalization. **Side-effect:** writes the normalized address lines and composed `address` back onto the body and republishes it.\n\n3. **ValidateOwnerPostcode** \u2014 optional field. If a postcode is present: must be exactly 4 digits; for a city with a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099) it must be in range; unknown-region cities accept any 4-digit code. Malformed/out-of-range throws `InvalidPostcodeException` (**400**). Absent postcode is untouched.\n\n4. **ValidateOwnerRegistrationDate** \u2014 optional field. If `registrationDate` is later than the server's current date, throws `FutureRegistrationDateException` (**400**). Absent is not checked.\n\n5. **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** \u2014 converts telephone to E.164 (strip spaces/dashes/brackets; keep leading `+`/country code, else assume `+61` and drop a single leading `0`; result must be 8\u201315 digits). **Side-effect:** writes E.164 value back onto the body. Invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (**400**).\n\n6. **NormalizeOwnerEmail** \u2014 optional. If present: trim + lower-case, must match the email regex, and its domain must not be on the disposable blocklist (mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com). **Side-effect:** writes lower-cased email back. Invalid/disposable \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (**400**). Null/blank passes through untouched.\n\n7. **EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity** *(transaction)* \u2014 unless the request opts in with `sharesHousehold: true` (which bypasses the whole check), scans all owners (skipping soft-deleted ones) and rejects with `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**) on either a **household duplicate** (same deterministic householdId = lastName + postcode) or a **contact duplicate** (same normalized telephone + email).\n\n8. **EnsureCityBelowCapacity** *(transaction)* \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed); if \u2265 50, rejects with `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**).\n\n9. **EnsureBelowDailyLimit** *(transaction)* \u2014 computes the effective registration date (supplied or server date) rolled onto a business day; if \u2265 100 owners already exist for that business day, rejects with `DailyOwnerLimitException` (**429**).\n\n10. **BuildOwner** *(transaction)* \u2014 maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity; defaults `registrationDate` to today when absent and adjusts it forward onto a business day. **Side-effect:** produces the entity.\n\n11. **AssignOwnerHousehold** *(transaction)* \u2014 **side-effect:** sets `householdId` = deterministic hash of (lastName, postcode).\n\n12. **AssignCustomerCode** *(transaction)* \u2014 **side-effect:** sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city, hash of normalizedTelephone + lastName), appending `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 to resolve collisions with existing codes.\n\n13. **CountNamesakes** *(transaction)* \u2014 **side-effect:** sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n14. **CountHouseholdMembers** *(transaction)* \u2014 **side-effect:** sets `householdSize` = existing owners sharing the same householdId, plus this one.\n\n15. **FlagPossibleDuplicate** *(transaction)* \u2014 **side-effect:** (skipped, set false/null, when `sharesHousehold: true`) sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` when a non-deleted existing owner shares lastName (case-insensitive) + postcode but has a different telephone; records the lowest matching id.\n\n16. **SaveOwner** *(transaction)* \u2014 **side-effect:** persists the owner via the repository (assigns its id).\n\n17. **AuditOwnerCreated** *(transaction)* \u2014 **side-effect:** emits an `AUDIT` log line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, and derived membershipLevel/membershipNumber.\n\n18. **EvaluateBulkSignupWarning** *(transaction)* \u2014 **side-effect:** sets the transient `bulkSignupWarning` flag true when > 80 owners share the same business-day registrationDate.\n\n19. **RecordIdempotencyKey** *(transaction)* \u2014 **side-effect:** if the request carried an `Idempotency-Key`, records key \u2192 new owner id in the store (so future repeats replay).\n\n20. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** *(transaction)* \u2014 **side-effect:** maps to `OwnerDto` and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n### Notes on ordering rationale\n- Validations run **cheapest/most-specific first**: required fields \u2192 postcode \u2192 registration date \u2192 telephone/email normalization \u2192 uniqueness/capacity/rate limits, so a bad body yields **400** before any duplicate/capacity **409/429** check touches the repository.\n- The three normalization steps (2, 5, 6) are both validation *and* side-effect: they mutate the request body in place so all later duplicate checks, persistence, and the response use the canonical forms.\n- Steps 7\u201320 all share `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the whole create commits once at the end."
